# Line endings are LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every platform. Two reasons:
#
# 1. `.githooks/*` are `#!/bin/sh` scripts git executes directly. A checkout that rewrote
#    them with CRLF endings would hand the shell a carriage return as part of the
#    interpreter path, which fails as if the hook were broken.
# 2. The engine writes every generated file - README.md, the radar page, snapshots, field
#    reports - with LF endings, and the generated CI runs on Linux and on Windows. A
#    checkout that converted them would show each one as changed on the machine that did
#    not create it.
* text=auto eol=lf
